Hi,
I'm trying an "imitation" of JGR in my Java app for very basics functions.
I plan to make a Deducer plugin later, for advanced users
YET :
I Have JRI installed, I have a Rengine object working and the eval function.
I use it to load rJava and JavaGD and then launch JavaGD().
So I get charts and every R command working from Java, so far so good, 
just like JGR.
BUT :
When I install iFlow and then launch iFlow with library(iFlow) it shows 
an empty window frame.
iFlow is downloadable here if you want to reproduce this bug :
http://www.bioconductor.org/packages/2.6/bioc/html/iFlow.html

So i thought it was a problem between JRI and RGTK2, so I did the same 
library(iFlow) in JGR thinking it would fail and ... it worked!
Why? What is there in JGR that I missed in JRI?

Thanks for all guys, JGR is great, and I love Deducer and iplots and 
Acinonyx. I know my question is about JRI and not about JGR itself so I 
won't get upset if nobody answers.

