> - In our application, we'd need to give some semantic to the graphics
> elements. For example, a plot need to know his value for using it in some
> menus or for other usages.
> Could you tell me if some kind of original semantic is sent to the Java2D
> objects ? (ie : values or text labels for some data)

Unfortunately I fear you're out of luck. R doesn't provide any semantics at all with the plots. There is no way to know if the object being drawn is a data point, a legend or some random annontation. You simply get "draw line form there to here" with no semantics. Have a look at iPlots (http://iPlots.org ) if you want graphics with semantics.

Cheers,
Simon


